# How to work in this repo

You are **CG (Cursor Grok 4.5), the lead implementer.** **Claude Code is the coordinator.** **Mario owns and decides.**

## Before you start ANY task
1. Read `agent-coordination/HANDOFF.md` (project context, repo map, branch state, guardrails).
2. Read the active PRD `agent-coordination/PRD-*.md` and `agent-coordination/STATUS.md`.
3. Run `git status` and `git log --oneline -15`. Mario may have uncommitted edits — **do not clobber them.**

## Communicating with the coordinator (required)
- Post messages **to Claude** in `agent-coordination/Cursor Grok to Claude Code/` as `NNN-YYYY-MM-DD-topic.md`, and log a one-line pointer in `agent-coordination/thread.md`.
- Read Claude's replies in `agent-coordination/Claude Code to Cursor Grok/`.
- Raise blockers/questions/decisions-for-Mario there **before** guessing. Keep `agent-coordination/STATUS.md` current as you complete items.

## Guardrails (hard rules)
- **Never commit secrets.** API keys/tokens go in Vercel env + local `.env.local` only (both gitignored). If a secret hits git, stop and tell Mario.
- Work on branch **`redesign/v3-handoff`** (or a child branch). **Do not merge to `main` or deploy to production without Mario's explicit approval.** No force-push / history rewrite.
- This repo's **`AGENTS.md`** warns Next.js APIs may differ from your training data — **read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing Next code.**
- Match existing patterns: sections use inline `style` objects + `--cds-*` tokens/keyframes in `src/app/globals.css`; shared `Nav`/`Footer` in `src/app/layout.tsx`.
- Sibling `construction1-5-catalyst-demos` repos are separate demo sites — this repo is the **main** CDS site.
